50. STRING CONCATENATION MANUALLY
------------------------------------------------------------

void append(char dest[], size_t capacity, const char src[])
{
    size_t d = strlen(dest);
    size_t s = 0;

    if (d >= capacity)
        return;

    while (src[s] != '\0' && d + 1 < capacity)
    {
        dest[d++] = src[s++];
    }

    dest[d] = '\0';
}


This demonstrates explicit capacity handling.

A production API should clearly specify what happens when the
source does not fit.


------------------------------------------------------------
51. STRING COPY MANUALLY
------------------------------------------------------------

void copyString(char dest[],
                size_t capacity,
                const char src[])
{
    if (capacity == 0)
        return;

    size_t i = 0;

    while (src[i] != '\0' && i + 1 < capacity)
    {
        dest[i] = src[i];
        i++;
    }

    dest[i] = '\0';
}


This copies at most:

capacity - 1

characters and always terminates when capacity > 0.


