52. BUFFER OVERFLOW
------------------------------------------------------------

One of the most important C security issues.

Example:

char name[10];

gets(name);


`gets()` is removed from the C standard because it cannot
safely limit input size.

NEVER use gets().


Use:

fgets(name, sizeof name, stdin);


instead.


------------------------------------------------------------
53. BUFFER OVERFLOW EXAMPLE
------------------------------------------------------------

char name[10];

scanf("%s", name);


Input:

ThisIsAVeryLongName


The input may exceed the array capacity.

Result:

undefined behavior and possible memory corruption.


Better:

scanf("%9s", name);


or use fgets() for line input.


